      <species id="mwd1bfc325_a757_416c_b673_ce4dbff773a2" name="qPSC" compartment="mw54522d8d_fbae_4c22_a771_a99c40ce0fb3" initialAmount="0" substanceUnits="MWUSERUNIT_cell" hasOnlySubstanceUnits="true" boundaryCondition="false" constant="false">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Quiescent pancreatic stellate cells in tumor compartment. In normal pancreas, PSCs store vitamin A and maintain stromal homeostasis.</body>
        </notes>
      </species>
      <species id="mw7d847991_7710_4efe_9f91_a662ca270b07" name="iCAF" compartment="mw54522d8d_fbae_4c22_a771_a99c40ce0fb3" initialAmount="0" substanceUnits="MWUSERUNIT_cell" hasOnlySubstanceUnits="true" boundaryCondition="false" constant="false">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Inflammatory cancer-associated fibroblasts. Secrete IL-6 and CXCL12, driving MDSC recruitment, M2 polarization, and CXCR4-mediated T-cell exclusion (Elyada 2019, Ogawa 2021). Driven by tumor-derived IL-1alpha; TGFb antagonizes via IL-1R1 repression.</body>
        </notes>
      </species>
      <species id="mw077f3787_2ba0_40e1_b35a_27aa59821e53" name="myCAF" compartment="mw54522d8d_fbae_4c22_a771_a99c40ce0fb3" initialAmount="0" substanceUnits="MWUSERUNIT_cell" hasOnlySubstanceUnits="true" boundaryCondition="false" constant="false">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Myofibroblastic cancer-associated fibroblasts. Secrete ECM (collagen), TGFb, VEGF. Build desmoplastic barrier. Favored by TGFb signaling (Biffi 2019). (CXCL12 is iCAF-derived, not myCAF -- audit m2-A-ECM-01.)</body>
        </notes>
      </species>
      <species id="mw3b53b1ff_a185_40cb_81e8_5c1b6456ebac" name="apCAF" compartment="mw54522d8d_fbae_4c22_a771_a99c40ce0fb3" initialAmount="0" substanceUnits="MWUSERUNIT_cell" hasOnlySubstanceUnits="true" boundaryCondition="false" constant="false">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Antigen-presenting cancer-associated fibroblasts. Express MHC-II, present tumor antigen tolerogenically -&gt; Treg induction. Rarest subtype ~2-5% of CAFs (Elyada 2019).</body>
        </notes>
      </species>
      <species id="mw97140954_e511_45d6_b5fd_d484c3f3da5d" name="collagen" compartment="mw54522d8d_fbae_4c22_a771_a99c40ce0fb3" initialAmount="0" substanceUnits="MWBUILTINPREFIX_milli_MWBUILTINUNIT_gram" hasOnlySubstanceUnits="true" boundaryCondition="false" constant="false">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Fibrillar collagen (types I/III) in tumor (total mass in mg). Primary structural ECM component driving desmoplasia. Determines pore size (immune exclusion) and stiffness (mechanotransduction).</body>
        </notes>
      </species>
